# ── SPA catch-all REMOVED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Previously: /*  /index.html  200
#
# This was causing ALL unknown URLs to return HTTP 200 instead of 404,
# making it impossible for search engines to detect missing pages.
#
# It is no longer needed because the prerender plugin now emits BOTH:
#   dist/<slug>/index.html  →  serves /<slug>/  (200, canonical trailing-slash)
#   dist/<slug>.html        →  serves /<slug>   (200, no redirect needed)
#
# Valid routes all have prerendered files and work at 200 without this rule.
# Unknown routes now correctly return 404 and serve public/404.html.
